      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/adam/{size}/1946_2.png",
      "created_at": "2011-08-17T09:16:37.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>There’s technically a table-uniqueness rule, so while you could have both Legacy decks in play, their abilities and equipment will have to be highly focused. As discussed on another thread, you could do a house-rules thing and use both of them - you’d just have to watch out for multiple copies of things like Lead from the Front. It’s not considered balanced to use both of them, and you couldn’t do so in a tournament, but for the flavor of it in your own private games, feel free. <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"></p>",
